sycl: decode-size f32 GEMVs take the small-matmul kernel

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0010.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

At decode Inkling multiplies small f32 matrices by one token many times per
token: the MoE router [2304 x 128], the relative-bias table and the K/V
rotation matrices (the loop controller's are fused by 0019). The generic
MUL_MAT path spent 15-19 us of host time on each, where a plain parallel_for
costs about 5 us. A 2-D f32 product with at most 32 columns and at most
2^20 MACs now takes 0004's small-matmul kernel. With K >= 64 and 16-byte
aligned rows, a work-group per output splits K across float4 loads.
Hadamard-hinted products keep their transform.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
index 58cf7be81..9c6f72a9c 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
@@ -5194,7 +5194,9 @@ static bool can_use_mul_mat_q(const ggml_tensor * src0, const ggml_tensor * src1
 
